@startuml offchain-vs-onchain
!theme mars
title Off-chain vs On-chain Responsibilities

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam padding 4

package "Off-chain (PostgreSQL)" as OFFCHAIN #1e3a5f {
    component "Purchase handling" as OC1
    component "Cashback calculation\n& business rules" as OC2
    component "Event orchestration\n(Outbox Pattern)" as OC3 #f97316
    component "Retry & failure handling" as OC4
    component "Off-chain ledger\n(cashback_ledger)" as OC5
}

package "Boundary" as BOUNDARY #4a1d96 {
    component "cashback.approved\n(NATS event)" as B1
    component "MintToken\n(gRPC call)" as B2
}

package "On-chain (Ethereum)" as ONCHAIN #065f46 {
    component "Token minting" as ON1
    component "Token ownership\n(wallet balances)" as ON2
    component "Immutable audit trail\n(tx history)" as ON3
}

OFFCHAIN -right-> BOUNDARY
BOUNDARY -right-> ONCHAIN

note bottom of OFFCHAIN
  Off-chain systems **decide**
  what should happen.
end note

note bottom of ONCHAIN
  On-chain systems **guarantee**
  the final and auditable state.
end note

@enduml

